    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d520">

                <pb facs="0520" n="1254" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1254"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Mr.
                            Terrell.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-01-26"><hi rendition="#italic">January 26,
                        1895</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 328.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    Nos. 376 and 386, of the respective dates of December 20, 1894, and January 7,
                    1895, relating to the unauthorized search of Bev. Mr. Lee’s house in Marash, and
                    to commend the promptness and firmness of your actions therein reported.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin F. Uhl</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
